whyItStood:
Could not refute — the path traces end to end in the real bytes, with no guard anywhere.

(1) HANDLER IS LIVE: `_bindInput()` is invoked from the constructor at game.js:199, and its last statement is game.js:469 `window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => this._onKey(e));`. Active in every state including TITLE.

(2) CLAIMED CODE IS VERBATIM CORRECT, game.js:476-482:
    if (this.hud.overlayOpen) {
      if (k === 'Escape' || k === 'Enter') {
        const b = this.hud.ovInner.querySelector('.btn.primary');
        if (b) { b.click(); e.preventDefault(); }
      }
      return;
    }
The `return` fires before game.js:490 `if (k === 'Escape') { this.openMenu(); return; }` — which is the game's own proof that Escape is bound to back/cancel everywhere else. The overlay branch inverts that meaning.

(3) SELECTOR PICKS THE DESTRUCTIVE BUTTON: confirmWipe() at game.js:818-834 emits, in order, `<button class="btn" data-a="no">No</button>` then `<button class="btn primary" data-a="yes">Break it</button>`. `.btn.primary` requires both classes, so it cannot match "No" (class="btn" only) and matches exactly "Break it". No key is bound to "No" at all.

(4) .click() REACHES A REAL LISTENER: hud.bind (hud.js:883-887) is `const e = this.ovInner.querySelector(sel); if (e) e.addEventListener('click', fn);`, attached at game.js:829 AFTER openOverlay sets innerHTML, so it is on the live node. HTMLElement.click() dispatches a click event that runs it.

(5) DAMAGE IS UNRECOVERABLE: the handler runs SaveIO.wipe() -> save.js:115-116 `export function wipe() { try { localStorage.removeItem(KEY); } catch (e) {} }`, then blankSave() and showTitle(). Shelf, codex, standing and ash-marks are gone with no undo.

(6) NO GUARD EXISTS: grep for `keydown|keyup|stopPropagation|Escape` across all of src/ returns only game.js:469, 477, 490 and main.js:156 (a `{once:true}` audio-resume kick, unrelated). No capture-phase handler, no overlay-local listener, no focus trap, no stopPropagation. openOverlay (hud.js:869-874) only sets innerHTML and toggles classes; `get overlayOpen()` (hud.js:881) returns true whenever class 'on' is present, which confirmWipe's openOverlay sets.

(7) REACHABLE, AND ONLY WHEN IT HURTS: showTitle() at game.js:792 computes `const fresh = s.day === 1 && s.rep === 0 && s.gallery.length === 0;` and renders the wipe entry only under `${fresh ? '' : '<button data-a="wipe">...'}`. The button therefore appears ONLY when the player has real progress to lose. Desktop browsers are a stated target platform, so Escape is reachable by definition (and iPad hardware keyboards send it too).

(8) SECONDARY CLAIM ALSO HOLDS: game.js:2579 makes `<button class="btn primary" data-a="next">` the primary on the results card; its listener (game.js:2591-2594) does `this.hud.closeOverlay()` then `nextCommission()`. Escape on the report you are reading closes it and advances the day.

REPRO CONFIRMED: play at least one day so `fresh` is false -> title screen -> click "Break everything and start again" -> confirmation appears -> press Escape -> save erased, back at a blank title screen.

The only defense of the current design is "Enter or Escape = default action", but that is precisely the defect: the branch treats Enter and Escape as interchangeable, which is fine on an informational overlay and wrong on the one screen that asks "Are you sure". Suggested fix: in the overlay branch, split the keys — Enter clicks `.btn.primary`, Escape prefers a cancel affordance (e.g. `[data-a="no"]`/`.btn.ghost`) and falls back to closing the overlay rather than firing the primary.

